[{"id":54612,"sender_id":56,"sender_full_name":"jamievicary","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/5d4cb43d795a03148f8552151d9af219?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Embedding.20a.20picture/near/54612\">#1</a> Hi,</p>\n<p>Can anyone tell me how to embed an image into an nLab page?</p>\n<p>Thanks,\nJamie</p>","timestamp":1448539557,"subject":"Embedding a picture","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":54613,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Embedding.20a.20picture/near/54613\">#2</a> Like the diagrams towards the bottom of <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Feynman%20diagram\">Feynman diagram</a>? You can see from the <a href=\"http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Feynman+diagram\">source</a> there the syntax: &lt;img …</p>\n<p>You can position images too, as in Urs’s photo at his <a href=\"http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber\">page</a>, <a href=\"http://ncatlab.org/nlab/source/Urs+Schreiber\">source</a>.</p>","timestamp":1448542045,"subject":"Embedding a picture","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":54618,"sender_id":56,"sender_full_name":"jamievicary","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/5d4cb43d795a03148f8552151d9af219?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Embedding.20a.20picture/near/54618\">#3</a> Perfect, thanks!</p>","timestamp":1448615320,"subject":"Embedding a picture","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":54619,"sender_id":13,"sender_full_name":"Tim_Porter","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f5067a77bfb4640f798f193b25d43eba?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Embedding.20a.20picture/near/54619\">#4</a> The picture IS a bit small! ;-) (see <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/globular\">globular</a>)</p>","timestamp":1448622259,"subject":"Embedding a picture","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":54620,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Embedding.20a.20picture/near/54620\">#5</a> Jamie, to add links within nLab you enclose terms in double square brackets. Assuming that’s what you wanted, I adjusted your single brackets.</p>","timestamp":1448625062,"subject":"Embedding a picture","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]},{"id":54625,"sender_id":56,"sender_full_name":"jamievicary","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/5d4cb43d795a03148f8552151d9af219?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/1-nLab/topic/Embedding.20a.20picture/near/54625\">#6</a> Thanks David and Tim :)</p>","timestamp":1448834084,"subject":"Embedding a picture","stream_id":1,"display_recipient":"nLab","reactions":[]}]